# Device: Unisoc Tiger T618 (UMS512)  Cortex-A75 + A55, Mali-G52 MP2
#
# A .device is an INTEGRATION unit, not a build unit: it names the ABI profile
# whose dist/ this device consumes.  Cores are built once per profile
# (gen-recipe.sh <profile>), never once per device.
#
# ARMv8.2-A, so the same profile as sm8250, a527 and rk3566.  The profile builds
# for the A55 baseline, which the A75 runs; per-board tuning is
# BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION's business, not the core builder's.

PROFILE aarch64-v8.2a

# GPU stack.  The emulators drop is keyed on PROFILE *and* this: emulators link
# the vendor GL stack, so a Mali payload cannot run on an Adreno board (it needs
# libmali.so.0, which such a board does not ship).  Cores are keyed on PROFILE
# alone -- they link only libGLESv2/libEGL, which both stacks provide.
GPU mali
